            <div xml:id="d448">

                <pb facs="0439" n="427" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg427"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.105A/8–1844: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Morris</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-12T12:00:00-04:00">September 12,
                            1944—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>552. Dept has informed Iranian Minister<anchor n="32" xml:id="d448-f1"/> that
                    this Government is agreeable to extension of agreement covering Schwarzkopf
                    Mission for period of one year effective October 2, 1944, provided the authority
                    given the President for detail of such officers remains in effect for that
                    period. Please inform Iranian Government.</p>
                <p>In reply to point raised in urtel 630 August 18 you may assure Schwarzkopf of the
                    permanent nature of our interest in Iran along lines given in Dept’s 462 July
                        31.<anchor n="33" xml:id="d448-f2"/> You may say that Dept will lend its
                    support to continuance of <hi rendition="#italic">Gendarmerie</hi> Mission until
                    it has accomplished its task or until it becomes clear that its presence in Iran
                    will no longer contribute to furtherance of American interests. However it
                    should be made clear that Mission’s continuance on present military basis is
                    limited by legislation. Dept will at appropriate time use its best endeavors
                    with War to obtain amendment of this limiting legislation or if that is not
                    possible will recommend continuance of Mission on civilian basis.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
